--TEST--
`Core\Http\Client::request` asks the two questions its named siblings answer while compiling, and throws before the first attempt rather than before the retry — `rule:http-server/a-non-idempotent-retry-needs-an-idempotency-key`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The verb is an argument here, so neither question can be put to the call
// site: at `::get` and `::post` a body on a bodyless verb and a keyless retry
// are compile-time diagnostics, and at `::request` they are the same two
// refusals made before anything is sent — which is what a test run finds,
// rather than production finding it on the one retry that matters. Nothing
// below opens a socket (`rule:testing/an-outbound-call-is-answered-from-a-table`).
Core\Test::answerHttp("https://api.example.com/*", 200, {body: "ok"});

// A body under a verb that carries none, then the same refusal at the other
// bodyless verb and a second key, so a check that learned one of either would
// pass here while still being wrong.
try {
    var $a = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "https://api.example.com/orders", {json: ["id" => 7]});
} catch (RuntimeError $bodied) {
    echo $bodied->message, "\n";
}
try {
    var $b = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Head, "https://api.example.com/orders", {body: "raw", contentType: "text/plain"});
} catch (RuntimeError $typed) {
    echo $typed->message, "\n";
}

// A repeated effect with no identity the server could recognise it by, asked of
// both verbs on that roster.
try {
    var $c = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Post, "https://api.example.com/orders", {json: ["id" => 7], retryAttempts: 3});
} catch (RuntimeError $keyless) {
    echo $keyless->message, "\n";
}
try {
    var $d = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Patch, "https://api.example.com/orders/7", {json: ["id" => 7], retryAttempts: 3});
} catch (RuntimeError $second) {
    echo $second->message, "\n";
}

// The bound on its other side: a body under a verb that carries one, a retry
// with the key it owes, and a `Get` that asks a question and nothing else.
var $e = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Put, "https://api.example.com/orders", {json: ["id" => 7]});
var $f = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Post, "https://api.example.com/orders", {json: ["id" => 7], retryAttempts: 3, retryIdempotencyKey: "order-7"});
var $g = Core\Http\Client::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "https://api.example.com/orders");

// Nothing that threw was sent — the records are the three calls that passed.
var $sent = Core\Test::sentHttp();
echo Core\Arr::count($sent), "\n";
foreach ($sent as Core\Test\SentRequest $call) {
    echo ($call->method() as int), " ", Core\Bytes::length($call->body()), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
Core\Http\Client::request: a `GET` sends no body, and `json` is one — put the value in the URL's query, or send it under a verb that carries a body
Core\Http\Client::request: a `HEAD` sends no body, and `body` is one — put the value in the URL's query, or send it under a verb that carries a body
Core\Http\Client::request: a repeated `POST` is a second effect rather than a second question, so retrying one needs `retryIdempotencyKey` in the same bag, sent as `Idempotency-Key` and identical across attempts
Core\Http\Client::request: a repeated `PATCH` is a second effect rather than a second question, so retrying one needs `retryIdempotencyKey` in the same bag, sent as `Idempotency-Key` and identical across attempts
3
5 8
4 8
0 0
